//@ run-pass
//@ timeout: 180
//@ expect-stdout-contains: CIRC28_DRUG_MIDAZOLAM_PASS
//
// Midazolam on the circ28 drug record (stdlib/darwin_pbpk/circ28_drug_midazolam.sio), round 3:
// POOLED fitted observables, two dose forms (solution, tablet), validation against study
// distributions. Parameter table, sources and statuses: header of the module.
//
// ROUND 5 (transit input and gut-wall Kp; read first; rounds 3 and 4 below are kept as the record of
// those rounds, and their first-order-absorption numbers are superseded where this block says so).
//   WHAT CHANGED. (1) Oral input: an Erlang chain of NTR = 4 stages (Brill 2014, Clin Pharmacokinet 53:931,
//   PMID 25141974, PMC4171595, full text read: three transit compartments, Ka = Ktr, so MTT = (n+1)/Ktr and
//   ntr = n + 1 = 4 stages in this record; rule 11 of the common rules). The record slot CD_KA is now the
//   rate k of ONE stage. k is refitted for each dose form to the SAME pooled Tmax as before (solution 0.4645 h,
//   tablet 0.9291 h; one observable per parameter, unchanged). tlag stays 0 (Brill: no lag, the chain replaces
//   it). Cmax, Cmax/AUC and the MTT are validation rows. MTT validation (NOT fitted, different populations):
//   Brill tablet, 20 morbidly obese patients, Ktr 0.057 /min, MTT 70.2 min = 1.17 h; Brill ORAL SOLUTION, 12
//   healthy volunteers, Ktr 0.130 /min, MTT 30.8 min = 0.51 h. (2) Gut-wall Kp: the module is run with BOTH
//   variants, gv 0 = the Rodgers-Rowland Kp of every organ times the V_ss scalar (all-organ, as in rounds 1-4),
//   gv 1 = the gut wall left at its Rodgers-Rowland Kp and the scalar refitted to V_ss in closed form
//   (circ28_kp_scale_for_vss_gutrr). Everything that depends on the scalar is refitted (clint_gut, clint,
//   both k). Section G prints the validation rows of both columns.
//   ADOPTION RULE (written before any run): the gut-unscaled variant is adopted only if (i) the largest |z|
//   among the peak rows (Q1, Q3, Q6, T1, T3, T6) that FAIL under gv 0 falls by more than 0.5, or one of them
//   changes from FAIL to PASS, (ii) no row of the whole table changes from PASS to FAIL, and (iii) AUC at 7.5 mg
//   moves by less than its standard uncertainty (it should not move: F and CL are fixed by the closed forms).
//   WHAT I HAD SEEN BEFORE WRITING THIS BLOCK (disclosure): tests/run-pass/circ28_transit_input.sio printed, for
//   THIS midazolam tablet record (all-organ, first-order fit), k for n = 2, 3, 5 stages (2.4555, 3.9431, 6.7665
//   /h) and Cmax/AUC for n = 1, 2, 3, 5 (0.2334, 0.3226, 0.3671, 0.4233). Nothing for n = 4, nothing for the
//   solution, nothing for the gut variant, no Cmax of any validation row with a transit input.
//   PREDICTIONS (point; range) FOR THE ntr = 4 RUN, gv 0 (all-organ):
//     k tablet 5.3 /h (4.9-5.8), MTT = 4/k 0.75 h (0.69-0.82): ratio to Brill's obese 1.17 h about 0.64, PASS at
//       fold 2 but not close (the model MTT is shorter).
//     k solution 13 /h (9-19), MTT 0.31 h (0.21-0.45): ratio to Brill's healthy 0.51 h about 0.6 (0.4-0.9);
//       PASS at fold 2 with about 65% confidence.
//     tablet Cmax/AUC 0.397 (0.38-0.415): T6 passes (z +0.8, was FAIL z -2.5); T1 Cmax 7.5 mg 41 (z +0.4) PASS;
//       T3 Cmax 15 mg 82 (z -0.2) PASS (was FAIL z -2.4); T2, T4, T7, T5 unchanged (AUC does not depend on k).
//     solution Cmax/AUC 0.58 (0.50-0.68): Q6 FAILS (observed 0.384, sb 0.046, z about +4: the transit peak is
//       too sharp for the solution); Q1 Cmax 7.5 mg 60 (z +0.8) PASS; Q3 Cmax 3 mg 24 (z +3.5) flips from
//       PASS to FAIL; Q2, Q4 (z 2.08 FAIL), Q5, Q7 unchanged.
//     AUC per mg 13.84 +/- 0.1 and oral t1/2 3.3 h unchanged; IV t1/2 3.31 h unchanged (3.29-3.33): an input
//       change cannot reach the IV run. E1 stays FAIL (3.31 against 2.06 h).
//     budget: u(AUC) 17.5% +/- 1 (CL 77%, Fg 21%); u(Cmax) tablet 18-25%, the Tmax share of its variance 5-15%.
//     compiled run time 2.0 s (1.5-3 s).
//   PREDICTIONS FOR gv 1 (gut unscaled, refitted): scalar within 5% of 0.839 (0.82-0.86, slightly lower: the
//     gut tissue holds 19% more); k of each form within 4% of the gv 0 value; Cmax/AUC within 3% of gv 0
//     (direction: down by about 1%, more gut hold-up); AUC within 0.3%; IV t1/2 3.31 +/- 0.08 h; NO verdict
//     changes anywhere. Therefore gv 1 is NOT adopted by the rule above (nothing it can move crosses a criterion).
//   OUTCOME OF THE ROUND-5 RUN (added after it; the predictions above are unchanged).
//     HIT: k tablet 5.372 /h (pred 5.3), MTT 0.745 h (0.75), k solution 12.24 /h (13), MTT 0.327 h (0.31), MTT ratios to
//       Brill 0.636 (tablet) and 0.641 (solution), both PASS at fold 2; tablet Cmax/AUC 0.3985 (0.397): T6 z +0.81 PASS
//       (was FAIL -2.57), T1 41.4 z +0.42, T3 82.7 z -0.16 PASS (was FAIL -2.42); solution Cmax/AUC 0.6065 (0.58): Q6
//       FAIL z +4.79, Q1 62.95 z +0.98 PASS, Q3 25.2 z +3.75 flips PASS -> FAIL; AUC per mg 13.84 unchanged; IV t1/2
//       3.312 h unchanged; budget u(AUC) 17.5%, CL 77%, Fg 21%; Tmax share of the tablet Cmax variance 13%; gv 1: scalar
//       0.8352, IV t1/2 3.298 h, AUC identical, no verdict change, rule says KEEP the all-organ scalar.
//     MISS: u(Cmax) tablet 15.4% (predicted 18-25%); k solution under gv 1 is 5.0% above gv 0 (predicted within 4%);
//       tablet Cmax/AUC under gv 1 is 0.7% HIGHER (predicted about 1% lower; the solution one is 0.4% lower);
//       compiled run time 1.6-3.5 s depending on machine load (predicted 2.0 s, 1.5-3): bound of 5 s held.
//     The stage count is what moves the peak (section S7): Cmax/AUC of the tablet 0.233, 0.323, 0.367, 0.398, 0.423 for
//     ntr 1-5 against an observed 0.359 (sb 0.049); the solution 0.375, 0.502, 0.564, 0.607, 0.639 against 0.384 (sb 0.046):
//     the SOLUTION passes only at ntr 1 and fails from ntr 2 on (z 2.5 at ntr 2), the tablet passes from ntr 2 on.
//     No single stage count fits both forms; the sourced ntr 4 (Brill) makes the tablet pass and the solution fail.
//
// ROUND 4 (read first; the round-3 text below it is kept as the record of that round, its Fg 0.57
// and its numbers are superseded where this block says so).
//   A. Fg is POOLED over Paine 1996, Thummel 1996, Gorski 1998, Hohmann 2015 (mdz_fg_studies; u =
//      max(SE_w, SE_b) as for CL; the round-3 reason for choosing one study, disagreement, is
//      between-study variance and is carried by SE_b). clint_gut, clint and both ka are refitted.
//   B. The IV half-life and the tablet peak shape are DIAGNOSED, not fitted: organ shares of the
//      body drug at 4, 8, 12 h; response to the ps scalar at 0.3, 1, 3.
//   PREDICTIONS WRITTEN BEFORE ANY KERNEL RUN OF THIS ROUND (closed forms and the pool evaluated in
//   Sounio, mdz_pool and mdz_fit; the kernel was not run on the new record):
//     coordinator: pooled Fg ~ 0.45 +/- 0.07; AUC per mg ~ 12.5; Q3, Q4 (Hohmann 3 mg) and T4 (tablet AUC
//       15 mg) move to |z| < 2; Qiu and Ahonen AUC drift negative but stay |z| < 2; oral F over six groups
//       improves.
//     mine: pooled Fg 0.4886 +/- 0.0419 (SE_w 0.0272, SE_b 0.0419, sb 0.0838, N 57), so u is the
//       between-study term; without Paine 0.481. Refit at the pool: Eg 0.1061, Eh 0.3140, F 0.3352,
//       AUC per mg 13.84 (119.8 -> 103.8 at 7.5 mg, 207.6 at 15 mg), clint_gut 261.2, clint 950.7,
//       kpsc 0.8390 (unchanged), ka 1.9768 /h solution and 0.8279 /h tablet (bisections on Tmax).
//       The coordinator's 12.5 per mg would need Fg ~ 0.44; the pool is 0.49, so I expect 13.8, not 12.5.
//       Rows: Q1 Cmax ~ 40 (pass), Q2 pass (z -0.55), Q3 Cmax 3 mg ~ 16 (z ~ 1.5, pass), Q4 AUC 3 mg ~ 41.5
//       (z ~ 2.1, still FAIL, marginal), T2 pass (z ~ 0.05), T3 Cmax 15 mg ~ 49 (z ~ -2.4, becomes a FAIL:
//       Cmax falls with F), T4 ~ 208 (z ~ 1.6, PASS), T6 tablet Cmax/AUC ~ 0.23 (FAIL), E1 IV t1/2 ~ 3.3
//       (FAIL, unchanged: Fg does not enter it), E7 oral F 0.335 (z ~ 0.7, pass).
//       Budget: u(AUC) ~ 14% (CL 10%, Fg 8.6% of 0.489), Cmax ~ 20%.
//     B (mine): the terminal phase is carried by adipose (> 50% of the body drug at 8 h) then muscle;
//       ps x 3 shortens the IV terminal t1/2 (to ~ 2.7 h, range 2.4-3.0) and raises the tablet Cmax/AUC (to ~ 0.26);
//       ps x 0.3 lengthens the t1/2 (~ 4.5 h) and lowers Cmax/AUC (~ 0.19). The ps scalar alone will not
//       reach the observed 2.06 h: a one-compartment limit has t1/2 = 0.693 Vss/CL = 1.92 h only at ps -> infinity.
//     Sourced early-IV observable: Heizmann 1983 (abstract): after a rapid IV injection the plasma
//       concentration fell to about 10% within 2 h. The model ratio C(2 h)/C(0.1 h) is printed against it.
//       No alpha half-life, V1 or digitised profile with full-text access was found, so ps is NOT fitted.
//   OUTCOME OF THE ROUND-4 RUN (added after the run, predictions above unchanged):
//     pooled Fg 0.4886 +/- 0.0419 as predicted (coordinator 0.45 +/- 0.07 was lower; u is the between-study term);
//     AUC per mg 13.84 (mine) not 12.5. Q3 z 1.38 pass (predicted ~1.5), Q4 z 2.08 still FAIL (predicted 2.1),
//     T3 z -2.42 became a FAIL (predicted -2.4), T4 z 1.61 PASS (predicted 1.6), T6 0.2334 FAIL, E1 3.31 h FAIL, E7 z 0.69
//     pass. Q1 Cmax came out 39.0 (predicted ~40), T1 Cmax 24.2 (z -0.56). Budget AUC 17.5% (predicted ~14%),
//     Cmax 20% solution / 18% tablet; CL carries 77% of var(AUC) now, Fg 21%.
//     B: adipose carries 69% (4 h) to 72% (12 h) of the body drug (predicted > 50%, held), muscle 10-11%.
//     MY ps PREDICTION WAS WRONG: ps x 0.3 / 1 / 3 moves the IV t1/2 only 3.47 / 3.31 / 3.27 h and the tablet
//     Cmax/AUC not at all (0.2334 / 0.2334 / 0.2335); ps/Q = 20 in every organ, exchange is not rate-limiting.
//     The slow tissue is adipose: kp 2.33, 15.3 L, Q 19.5 L/h, perfusion time constant kp Vt / (Q bp) = 2.7 h.
//     Model C(2 h)/C(0.1 h) = 0.22 against Heizmann's "about 10%": the early fall is too slow too.
//     Engine note: in lean_single mt_eh gave 0.3179 inside one function and 0.3140 in another (same record);
//     eh, eg, fg are now computed in main and passed in m[18..20]; the guard row compares Fg (1 - Eh)
//     with the F of the kernel runs.
//
// FITTED (so NOT validations). Pooled over the healthy-adult studies that give mean, SD, n
// (mdz_pool: n-weighted mean; u = max(pooled SE, between-study SD / sqrt(k)); the test prints
// every study and both terms):
//   plasma CL   Thummel 1996, Gorski 1998, Allonen 1981, Hohmann 2015       -> hepatic clint
//   V_ss        Heizmann 1983, Hohmann 2015                                  -> Kp scalar
//   Fg 0.57     ONE study, Paine 1996 (direct measurement; Thummel/Gorski mass-balance values
//               differ by 0.15 vs 2 SE = 0.147, so they are not pooled)       -> gut-wall clint
//   Tmax        solution: Hohmann 2015 + Smith 1981; tablet: Smith 1981 + Backman 1995 + Greenblatt
//               1986                                                          -> ka of the form
// DERIVED: ps_gut 10.454 L/h from Brussee 2018 (round 2). Not fitted.
// Left OUT of every fit, so these are validations: Qiu 2024 (all of it, including Tmax), Ahonen
// 1995 (all of it), the 15 mg Cmax/AUC groups, every oral F, the half-lives, Eh, Eg after IV.
// The Gorski CL and the Hohmann CL/Vss are now INPUTS of the pooled fit, so they are no longer
// validations (the round-2 row "IV CL vs Gorski" is gone).
//
// CRITERION. Row with one study and an inter-individual SD: |z| <= 2, z = (pred - obs)/SD (SD of
// individuals; a source's SEM is converted, SD = SEM sqrt(n); a geometric-mean CI gives
// SD = gm sqrt(n) (ln hi - ln lo)/(2 t), t = 2.1314; a CV is multiplied by the mean).
// Row with a DISTRIBUTION of studies (each group listed with mean and n): the prediction must lie
// within the n-weighted mean of the group means +/- 2 sb, sb = between-study SD (SD of the group
// means, k - 1). A failed row is reported as a failure and its discrepancy asserted in a band.
// Group weights that the abstract does not give (Lappin 2006, Greenblatt 1984) are set to n = 6
// and marked "assumed" in the printout. Formulation is stated for Qiu, Hohmann, Smith; for
// Ahonen, Backman and Greenblatt 1986 "tablet" is an assignment by dose strength and not read.
//
// WRITTEN BEFORE THE FIRST RUN OF THIS TEST. Closed forms evaluated in Sounio (mdz_pool, mdz_fit,
// circ28 extractions; no kernel run of the new model):
//   pooled CL 24.220 +/- 2.396 L/h, Vss 67.145 +/- 11.650 L, Tmax solution 0.4645 +/- 0.065 h,
//   tablet 0.9291 +/- 0.0936 h; kpsc 0.8390, clint_gut 188.26, clint 983.30 (Fg 0.57, ps_gut 10.454);
//   Eg(IV) 0.0892, Eh 0.3212, Fh 0.6788, F = Fg Fh = 0.3869, AUC = F Dose/CL = 15.97 ng h/mL per mg
//   (119.8 at 7.5 mg, 239.6 at 15 mg); with Fg 0.503 (Thummel+Gorski pool) F 0.344, 14.22 per mg;
//   with Fg 0.42 (Gorski) F 0.291, 12.00 per mg; with Fg 0.39 (Hohmann) F 0.271, 11.19 per mg.
//   ka solution 2.1572 /h, tablet 0.8525 /h: bisections on Tmax, no Cmax printed.
// ESTIMATES (not closed form; written before any Cmax or t1/2 of the new model was seen):
//   Cmax/AUC solution ~ 0.30 /h (0.25-0.38), tablet ~ 0.235 /h (0.21-0.27); so Cmax(7.5 mg) ~ 36
//   ng/mL solution (30-45) and ~ 28 tablet (25-32), Cmax(15 mg, tablet) ~ 56 (50-65); IV and oral
//   t1/2 ~ 3.1 h (2.7-3.5; the larger fitted Vss, 67 vs 50 L, lengthens the terminal phase).
//
//  row                                    predicted   observed (source)                          expected
//  Q1  solution Cmax 7.5 mg (ng/mL)       ~36         43.97 +/- 19.3 SD (Qiu 2024, CV 44%)       pass
//  Q2  solution AUC 7.5 mg (ng h/mL)      119.8       127.9 +/- 43.5 SD (Qiu 2024, CV 34%)       pass (z -0.19)
//  Q3  solution Cmax 3 mg                 ~14.4       9.99 +/- 4.05 SD (Hohmann 2015)            pass
//  Q4  solution AUC 3 mg                  47.9        24.4 +/- 8.2 SD (Hohmann 2015)             FAIL (z 2.86)
//  Q5  solution Tmax (h)                  0.4645 fit  0.51 median (Qiu 2024; not fitted)         pass, fold 2
//  Q6  solution Cmax/AUC (1/h)            ~0.30       0.344 (n 10), 0.409 (n 16): distribution   borderline (estimate)
//  Q7  solution oral t1/2 (h)             ~3.1        5.27 (n 10), 3.96 (n 16): distribution     pass
//  T1  tablet Cmax 7.5 mg                 ~28         34 +/- 17.3 SD (Ahonen 1995)               pass
//  T2  tablet AUC 7.5 mg                  119.8       102 +/- 34.6 SD (Ahonen 1995)              pass (z 0.51)
//  T3  tablet Cmax 15 mg                  ~56         100.7 (6), 86 (10), 70.4 (7): distribution borderline (mean 85.1, sb 15.2)
//  T4  tablet AUC 15 mg                   239.6       175 (7), 170 (10), 200 (9): distribution    FAIL (mean 181.7, sb 16.1, z 3.6)
//  T5  tablet Tmax (h)                    0.9291 fit  1.25 median (Ahonen 1995; not fitted)      pass, fold 2
//  T6  tablet Cmax/AUC (1/h)              ~0.235      0.333 (n 12), 0.402 (n 7): distribution    FAIL (estimate)
//  T7  tablet oral t1/2 (h)               ~3.1        3.8 (12), 3.1 (7), 3.24 (6): distribution  pass
//  E1  IV t1/2 (h)                        ~3.1        2.3 (6), 2.107 (8), 1.77 (6): distribution FAIL (estimate)
//  E2  gut extraction after IV            0.0892      0.08 +/- 0.11 SD (Paine 1996)              pass
//  E3  Eh                                 0.3212      0.44 +/- 0.14 SD (Thummel 1996, abstract)  pass (z -0.85)
//  E4  Eh                                 0.3212      0.43 +/- 0.113 SD (Hohmann 2015)           pass (z -0.97)
//  E5  Fh = 1 - Eh                        0.6788      0.74 +/- 0.1 SD (Gorski 1998)              pass (z -0.61)
//  E6  Fg (fitted)                        0.57        0.42 +/- 0.2 (Gorski); 0.39 +/- 0.16 (Hohmann: 1 - ERG 0.61)  pass (fitted: studies agree)
//  E7  oral F, distribution of 6 groups   0.3869      0.209 (16), 0.22 (6*), 0.24 (8), 0.31 (16), 0.41 (6*), 0.36 (6*)
//                                                     mean 0.279, sb 0.082                        pass (z 1.32)
//  E8  oral F                             0.3869      0.31 +/- 0.1 SD (Gorski 1998)              pass (z 0.77)
//  E9  oral F                             0.3869      (1-0.44)(1-0.43) = 0.319 +/- 0.156 SD, Thummel 1996 abstract only: EH, EG imply it   pass
//  E10 dose proportionality 7.5 -> 15 mg  2 (identity of the linear model; Bornemann 1985 found Cmax and AUC proportional
//                                         between 7.5 and 15 mg, more than proportional at 30 mg: abstract only)
// The round-2 row "F vs Thummel 0.262" (a ratio of two mean clearances computed here) is replaced by E9.
// Also printed: the leave-one-out CL pool, the Fg agreement test, the gut-tissue residence time versus
// the absorption time, the sensitivity of F and AUC per mg to Fg (0.57, 0.503, 0.42, 0.39) and to ps_gut,
// and the uncertainty budget (refit-aware) for both forms. Predicted budget (before running): AUC(7.5 mg)
// 119.8 +/- ~26 (22%), carried by CL (u 10%) and Fg (u 14%); Cmax +/- 25-30%, carried by Tmax.
//
// OUTCOME OF THE FIRST RUN (added after the run; the predictions above are unchanged).
//   Where the written estimates were wrong: solution Cmax 7.5 mg was ~36, is 46.6 (Qiu 43.97, z 0.13,
//   pass); Cmax/AUC solution was ~0.30, is 0.389 (pass, z 0.10); Q3 (Hohmann 3 mg Cmax) was predicted
//   ~14.4 and PASS, it is 18.6 (ratio 1.86, z 2.13) and FAILS, so its expectation is now "fail" and
//   asserted in a band; IV t1/2 was ~3.1, is 3.31 (FAIL as predicted, z 4.7). Everything else landed
//   on its predicted side (T3 56.7 vs ~56, z -1.87, inside the 2 sb limit by 0.13 sb).
//   Residual failures, all asserted in bands: Q3 and Q4 (Hohmann 3 mg Cmax/AUC, model about 1.9x),
//   T4 (tablet AUC 15 mg, z 3.6), T6 (tablet Cmax/AUC 0.237 vs 0.359, z -2.5), E1 (IV t1/2 3.31 vs 2.06 h,
//   z 4.7). The common cause of Q3, Q4 and T4 is F = 0.387 against a cohort mean of 0.279: AUC per mg
//   15.97 against 8.1-17.1 observed. Not tuned.
//
// Marker CIRC28_DRUG_MIDAZOLAM_PASS.

use darwin_pbpk::circ28::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_kp::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug_midazolam::*
use math::pure::{exp, ln}

fn mt_abs(x: f64) -> f64 {
    if x < 0.0 { return 0.0 - x }
    return x
}

fn mt_rel(tag: string, got: f64, want: f64, tol: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let r = mt_abs(got - want) / mt_abs(want)
    print("  "); print(tag); print(": got "); print(got); print(" want "); print(want)
    print("  rel = "); println(r)
    if !(r <= tol) {
        println("  [FAIL]")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

// One validation row. sd > 0: criterion |z| <= 2; sd = 0: criterion within `fold`.
// expect: 1 pass, 0 fail, 2 borderline. band_lo..band_hi bound z (sd > 0) or the
// ratio pred/obs (sd = 0) of the measured discrepancy. Returns 1 if the test must fail.
fn mt_row(tag: string, pred: f64, obs: f64, sd: f64, fold: f64, expect: i32, band_lo: f64, band_hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var stat = pred / obs
    var pass = false
    if sd > 0.0 {
        stat = (pred - obs) / sd
        pass = mt_abs(stat) <= 2.0
    } else {
        pass = stat <= fold && stat >= 1.0 / fold
    }
    print("  "); print(tag); print(": predicted "); print(pred); print("  observed "); print(obs)
    print("  ratio "); print(pred / obs)
    if sd > 0.0 {
        print("  z "); print(stat)
    }
    if pass { print("  PASS") } else { print("  FAIL") }
    var bad = 0
    if stat < band_lo || stat > band_hi {
        print("  [outside the asserted band]")
        bad = 1
    }
    if expect == 1 && !pass {
        print("  [expected pass]")
        bad = 1
    }
    if expect == 0 && pass {
        print("  [expected fail]")
        bad = 1
    }
    println("")
    return bad
}

fn mt_name(i: i32) -> string {
    if i == 0 { return "logP" }
    if i == 1 { return "pKa1" }
    if i == 2 { return "fu" }
    if i == 3 { return "B:P" }
    if i == 4 { return "V_ss obs" }
    if i == 5 { return "CL_iv obs" }
    if i == 6 { return "Fg obs" }
    if i == 7 { return "Tmax obs" }
    return "ps_gut"
}

fn mt_rname(i: i32) -> string {
    if i == 0 { return "MW" }
    if i == 1 { return "logP" }
    if i == 2 { return "pKa1" }
    if i == 3 { return "pKa2" }
    if i == 4 { return "ion class" }
    if i == 5 { return "fu" }
    if i == 6 { return "B:P" }
    if i == 7 { return "clint (hep)" }
    if i == 8 { return "clform" }
    if i == 9 { return "clint (gut)" }
    if i == 10 { return "cl renal" }
    if i == 11 { return "cl plasma" }
    if i == 12 { return "Kp scalar" }
    if i == 13 { return "ps scalar" }
    if i == 14 { return "ka" }
    if i == 15 { return "fa" }
    if i == 16 { return "tlag" }
    return "ps gut"
}

// One kernel run per call, one scalar back: lean_single corrupts a frame that holds several
// large structs (Circ28Params, Circ28Dose, Circ28Run) at once, so each run lives in its own frame.
// mode 0: IV 1 mg; 1: oral 7.5 mg; 2: oral 15 mg. k: 0 AUC_inf, 1 Cmax, 2 Tmax, 3 t1/2, 4 balance.
// pssc < 0 keeps the record value.
fn mt_pick(r: &Circ28Run, k: i32) -> f64 {
    if k == 0 { return (*r).auc_inf }
    if k == 1 { return (*r).cmax }
    if k == 2 { return (*r).tmax }
    if k == 3 { return (*r).thalf }
    return (*r).balance_err
}

// Arrays are never passed by value and structs never reassigned (lean_single corrupts both):
// the parameter array is filled in the function that runs the kernel, one function per mode.
fn mt_fill(d: &Circ28Drug, pssc: f64, th: &![f64; 18]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var ti: i32 = 0
    while ti < 18 {
        (*th)[ti] = circ28_drug_value(d, ti)
        ti = ti + 1
    }
    if pssc >= 0.0 { (*th)[CD_PSSC] = pssc }
    return 0
}
fn mt_m0(d: &Circ28Drug, pssc: f64, k: i32, gv: i32) -> f64 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    mt_fill(d, pssc, &!th)
    var d2 = mdz_cfg_iv(1.0)
    let r = mdz_run_theta(th, d2, gv)
    return mt_pick(&r, k)
}
fn mt_m1(d: &Circ28Drug, pssc: f64, k: i32, gv: i32) -> f64 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    mt_fill(d, pssc, &!th)
    var d2 = mdz_cfg_oral(7.5)
    let r = mdz_run_theta(th, d2, gv)
    return mt_pick(&r, k)
}
fn mt_m2(d: &Circ28Drug, pssc: f64, k: i32, gv: i32) -> f64 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    mt_fill(d, pssc, &!th)
    var d2 = mdz_cfg_oral(15.0)
    let r = mdz_run_theta(th, d2, gv)
    return mt_pick(&r, k)
}

fn mt_eh(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = circ28_drug_params(d)
    var p2 = p
    return circ28_hepatic_extraction(p2)
}
fn mt_eg(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = circ28_drug_params(d)
    return circ28_gut_extraction(p)
}
fn mt_fg(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = circ28_drug_params(d)
    return circ28_gut_availability(p)
}
fn mt_clb(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = circ28_drug_params(d)
    return circ28_splanchnic_clearance(p) * p.bp
}
fn mt_qgut(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = circ28_drug_params(d)
    return p.q[8]
}

// A distribution row: the groups (mean, n) are printed; the prediction is compared with the
// n-weighted mean of the group means using the between-study SD sb (z = (pred - mean)/sb).
// expect: 1 pass, 0 fail, 2 no assertion of the verdict; [blo, bhi] bound z.
fn mt_dist(tag: string, pred: f64, m: &[f64; 8], n: &[f64; 8], k: i32, expect: i32, blo: f64, bhi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var s: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let q = mdz_pool(m, &s, n, k)
    var i: i32 = 0
    print("  "); println(tag)
    while i < k {
        print("      group "); print(i); print(": mean "); print((*m)[i]); print("  n "); println((*n)[i])
        i = i + 1
    }
    let z = (pred - q.mean) / q.sb
    var pass = mt_abs(z) <= 2.0
    print("      predicted "); print(pred); print("  pooled mean "); print(q.mean); print("  sb "); print(q.sb)
    print("  ratio "); print(pred / q.mean); print("  z "); print(z)
    if pass { print("  PASS") } else { print("  FAIL") }
    var bad = 0
    if z < blo || z > bhi {
        print("  [outside the asserted band]")
        bad = 1
    }
    if expect == 1 && !pass {
        print("  [expected pass]")
        bad = 1
    }
    if expect == 0 && pass {
        print("  [expected fail]")
        bad = 1
    }
    println("")
    return bad
}

// ---- the observed groups (mean, n) -------------------------------------------------------
// oral F: Hohmann 2015 3 mg solution 0.209 (16); Lappin 2006 7.5 mg 0.22 (n assumed 6);
// Kupferschmidt 1995 15 mg water 0.24 (8); Gorski 1998 4 mg 0.31 (16); Greenblatt 1984
// young men 0.41 and young women 0.36 (n assumed 6 each)
fn mt_l_f(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 0.209
    (*n)[0] = 16.0
    (*m)[1] = 0.22
    (*n)[1] = 6.0
    (*m)[2] = 0.24
    (*n)[2] = 8.0
    (*m)[3] = 0.31
    (*n)[3] = 16.0
    (*m)[4] = 0.41
    (*n)[4] = 6.0
    (*m)[5] = 0.36
    (*n)[5] = 6.0
    return 6
}
// Cmax after 15 mg oral (tablet), ng/mL: Greenblatt 1986 100.7 (6: three occasions, one group);
// Backman 1995 86 (10); Backman 1996 Epilepsia controls 70.4 (7)
fn mt_l_c15(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 100.7
    (*n)[0] = 6.0
    (*m)[1] = 86.0
    (*n)[1] = 10.0
    (*m)[2] = 70.4
    (*n)[2] = 7.0
    return 3
}
// AUC after 15 mg oral (tablet), ng h/mL = ug min/mL x 1000/60: Backman 1996 Epilepsia 10.5 (7);
// Backman 1996 CPT placebo phase 10.2 (10); Backman 1994 12 (9). The three papers are from one
// laboratory and are treated as independent groups.
fn mt_l_a15(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 10.5 * 1000.0 / 60.0
    (*n)[0] = 7.0
    (*m)[1] = 10.2 * 1000.0 / 60.0
    (*n)[1] = 10.0
    (*m)[2] = 12.0 * 1000.0 / 60.0
    (*n)[2] = 9.0
    return 3
}
// peak shape Cmax/AUC (1/h): solution Qiu 2024 43.97/127.9 (10), Hohmann 2015 9.99/24.4 (16)
fn mt_l_cas(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 43.97 / 127.9
    (*n)[0] = 10.0
    (*m)[1] = 9.99 / 24.4
    (*n)[1] = 16.0
    return 2
}
// tablet: Ahonen 1995 34/102 (12), Backman 1996 70.4/175 (7)
fn mt_l_cat(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 34.0 / 102.0
    (*n)[0] = 12.0
    (*m)[1] = 70.4 / 175.0
    (*n)[1] = 7.0
    return 2
}
// oral t1/2 (h): solution Qiu 5.27 (10), Hohmann 3.96 (16)
fn mt_l_hs(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 5.27
    (*n)[0] = 10.0
    (*m)[1] = 3.96
    (*n)[1] = 16.0
    return 2
}
// tablet: Ahonen 3.8 (12), Backman 1996 3.1 (7), Greenblatt 1986 mean of 3.04, 3.38, 3.30 (6)
fn mt_l_ht(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 3.8
    (*n)[0] = 12.0
    (*m)[1] = 3.1
    (*n)[1] = 7.0
    (*m)[2] = (3.04 + 3.38 + 3.30) / 3.0
    (*n)[2] = 6.0
    return 3
}
// IV t1/2 (h): Heizmann 1983 2.3 (6), Greenblatt 1986 mean of 2.25, 2.02, 2.05 (8),
// Smith 1981 1.77 (6, terminal)
fn mt_l_hiv(m: &![f64; 8], n: &![f64; 8]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    (*m)[0] = 2.3
    (*n)[0] = 6.0
    (*m)[1] = (2.25 + 2.02 + 2.05) / 3.0
    (*n)[1] = 8.0
    (*m)[2] = 1.77
    (*n)[2] = 6.0
    return 3
}

// each distribution row in its own function: small frames
fn mt_vd_f(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_f(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("E7 oral F, distribution (Hohmann, Lappin*, Kupferschmidt, Gorski, Greenblatt 1984 M*, F*; * n assumed)", pred, &m, &n, k, 1, 0.5, 2.0)
}
fn mt_vd_c15(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_c15(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("T3 tablet Cmax 15 mg (ng/mL), distribution", pred, &m, &n, k, 1, 0.0 - 1.0, 0.7)
}
fn mt_vd_a15(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_a15(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("T4 tablet AUC 15 mg (ng h/mL), distribution", pred, &m, &n, k, 1, 0.5, 2.0)
}
fn mt_vd_cas(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_cas(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("Q6 solution Cmax/AUC (1/h), distribution", pred, &m, &n, k, 0, 4.0, 5.6)
}
fn mt_vd_cat(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_cat(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("T6 tablet Cmax/AUC (1/h), distribution", pred, &m, &n, k, 1, 0.3, 1.5)
}
fn mt_vd_hs(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_hs(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("Q7 solution oral t1/2 (h), distribution", pred, &m, &n, k, 1, 0.0 - 2.0, 0.0)
}
fn mt_vd_ht(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_ht(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("T7 tablet oral t1/2 (h), distribution", pred, &m, &n, k, 1, 0.0 - 2.0, 2.0)
}
fn mt_vd_hiv(pred: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    let k = mt_l_hiv(&!m, &!n)
    return mt_dist("E1 IV t1/2 (h), distribution (Heizmann, Greenblatt 1986, Smith)", pred, &m, &n, k, 0, 2.5, 8.0)
}

// print one pooled observable: studies, then the pool
fn mt_prt(tag: string, m: &[f64; 8], s: &[f64; 8], n: &[f64; 8], k: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var i: i32 = 0
    print("  "); println(tag)
    while i < k {
        print("      study "); print(i); print(": mean "); print((*m)[i]); print("  SD "); print((*s)[i]); print("  n "); println((*n)[i])
        i = i + 1
    }
    let q = mdz_pool(m, s, n, k)
    print("      pooled mean "); print(q.mean); print("  N "); print(q.n_tot); print("  k "); print(q.k)
    print("  sw "); print(q.sw); print("  SE_w "); print(q.se_w); print("  sb "); print(q.sb); print("  SE_b "); print(q.se_b)
    print("  u = max "); println(q.u)
    return 0
}

fn mt_sec_pool() -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S0 pooled observables: u = max(sw/sqrt(N), sb/sqrt(k)); sb = SD of the study means")
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var s: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var k = mdz_cl_studies(&!m, &!s, &!n)
    mt_prt("plasma CL (L/h): Thummel 1996, Gorski 1998, Allonen 1981, Hohmann 2015 (SD from the 95% CI)", &m, &s, &n, k)
    let pc = mdz_pool_cl()
    fails = fails + mt_rel("pooled CL = (20 x 22.2 + 16 x 28 + 6 x 16.98 + 16 x 25.68)/58 (hand arithmetic)", pc.mean, (20.0 * 22.2 + 16.0 * 28.0 + 6.0 * 16.98 + 16.0 * 25.68) / 58.0, 1.0e-12)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("pooled CL u (pinned)", pc.u, 2.395793, 1.0e-5)
    // leave-one-out: drop Allonen (slot 2), whose "+/-" is only assumed to be an SD
    m[2] = m[3]
    s[2] = s[3]
    n[2] = n[3]
    let q3 = mdz_pool(&m, &s, &n, 3)
    print("      leave-one-out without Allonen: pooled mean "); print(q3.mean); print("  u "); println(q3.u)
    k = mdz_vss_studies(&!m, &!s, &!n)
    mt_prt("V_ss (L): Heizmann 1983 (no SD in the abstract), Hohmann 2015", &m, &s, &n, k)
    let pv = mdz_pool_vss()
    fails = fails + mt_rel("pooled Vss mean (pinned)", pv.mean, 67.145455, 1.0e-6)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("pooled Vss u (pinned)", pv.u, 11.65, 1.0e-6)
    k = mdz_tmax_studies(0, &!m, &!s, &!n)
    mt_prt("Tmax solution (h): Hohmann 2015 (SD = range/sqrt12), Smith 1981", &m, &s, &n, k)
    k = mdz_tmax_studies(1, &!m, &!s, &!n)
    mt_prt("Tmax tablet (h): Smith 1981, Backman 1995 (SD = range/sqrt12), Greenblatt 1986 (no SD)", &m, &s, &n, k)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("Tmax solution mean (pinned)", mdz_obs_tmax(0), 0.464545, 1.0e-6)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("Tmax tablet mean (pinned)", mdz_obs_tmax(1), 0.929091, 1.0e-6)
    // Fg, pooled over four studies (round 4): the table, the pool, the pool without Paine (the only direct
    // measurement; the other three infer Fg from F, CL_iv and an assumed hepatic flow), and the agreement
    // of the studies as information (it no longer decides anything: disagreement is the SE_b term)
    k = mdz_fg_studies(&!m, &!s, &!n)
    mt_prt("Fg: Paine 1996 (direct), Thummel 1996, Gorski 1998, Hohmann 2015 (derived; mean of 3 ug and 3 mg)", &m, &s, &n, k)
    let pf = mdz_pool_fg()
    fails = fails + mt_rel("pooled Fg (pinned)", pf.mean, 0.488596, 1.0e-5)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("pooled Fg u (pinned, = SE_b)", pf.u, 0.041908, 1.0e-4)
    m[0] = m[1]
    s[0] = s[1]
    n[0] = n[1]
    m[1] = m[2]
    s[1] = s[2]
    n[1] = n[2]
    m[2] = m[3]
    s[2] = s[3]
    n[2] = n[3]
    let q3f = mdz_pool(&m, &s, &n, 3)
    print("      pool without Paine (three derived values): mean "); print(q3f.mean); print("  u "); println(q3f.u)
    let se_pg = cd_sqrt(0.18 * 0.18 / 5.0 + 0.2 * 0.2 / 16.0)
    let se_tg = cd_sqrt(0.24 * 0.24 / 20.0 + 0.2 * 0.2 / 16.0)
    print("  Fg study agreement |diff| / (2 SE): Paine vs Gorski "); print(0.15 / (2.0 * se_pg)); print("  Thummel vs Gorski "); println(0.15 / (2.0 * se_tg))
    println("      (a ratio > 1 means the two do not agree within 2 SE: that is between-study variance and is in u)")
    return fails
}

fn mt_sec_fit(d: &Circ28Drug, m: &![f64; 24], gv: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S1 parameter record (value, standard uncertainty, status); the ka row is the TABLET at this point")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 18 {
        print("  "); print(i); print(" "); print(mt_rname(i)); print("  value "); print(circ28_drug_value(d, i))
        print("  u "); print(cd_sqrt(circ28_drug_variance(d, i))); print("  status "); println((*d).status[i])
        i = i + 1
    }
    print("  ka solution "); print((*m)[17]); print("  u "); print((*m)[16]); print(" /h;  ka tablet "); print(circ28_drug_value(d, CD_KA)); println(" /h")
    println("S1b the fits reproduce their observables (these are NOT validations)")
    fails = fails + mt_rel("V_ss (L) = pooled", mt_vss(d, gv), mdz_obs_vss(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("plasma CL (L/h) = pooled", mt_clb(d), mdz_obs_cl(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("Fg = pooled Fg", mt_fg(d), mdz_obs_fg(), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("solution Tmax (grid and vertex) = pooled 0.4645 h", (*m)[6], mdz_obs_tmax(0), 2.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("tablet Tmax (grid and vertex) = pooled 0.9291 h", (*m)[11], mdz_obs_tmax(1), 2.0e-3)
    return fails
}

fn mt_vss(d: &Circ28Drug, gv: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = mdz_params_rec(d, gv)
    return circ28_vss_plasma(p)
}

fn mt_sec_iv(d: &Circ28Drug, m: &![f64; 24], gv: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let fg = (*m)[18]
    let eh = (*m)[19]
    print("S2 IV 1 mg: AUC_inf "); print((*m)[0]); print(" (Dose/CL = "); print(1.0 / mdz_obs_cl()); print(")  t1/2 "); print((*m)[2])
    print("  Cmax "); print((*m)[1]); print("  balance "); println((*m)[3])
    let mrt = mt_vss(d, gv) / mt_clb(d)
    print("  IV disposition shape: MRT = Vss/CL "); print(mrt); print(" h;  a single exponential with the model t1/2 would have MRT = 1.4427 t1/2 = ")
    print(1.4427 * (*m)[2]); println(" h (MRT well below that: a slow terminal phase from the peripheral compartments)")
    fails = fails + mt_rel("IV AUC_inf = Dose / CL", (*m)[0], 1.0 / mdz_obs_cl(), 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("oral mass balance (solution)", (*m)[8] + 1.0, 1.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("oral mass balance (tablet)", (*m)[13] + 1.0, 1.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("F from the IV and solution runs = Fg (1 - Eh)", ((*m)[4] / 7.5) / (*m)[0], fg * (1.0 - eh), 2.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("F from the IV and tablet runs = Fg (1 - Eh)", ((*m)[9] / 7.5) / (*m)[0], fg * (1.0 - eh), 2.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("AUC is the same for both forms (F does not depend on the rate; quadrature differs)", (*m)[9], (*m)[4], 1.0e-3)
    return fails
}

fn mt_sec_sol(m: &![f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("V1 SOLUTION (ka fitted to the pooled solution Tmax; Qiu 2024 is not in any fit)")
    let auc = (*m)[4] * 1000.0
    let cmax = (*m)[5] * 1000.0
    fails = fails + mt_row("Q1 Cmax 7.5 mg (ng/mL) Qiu 2024        ", cmax, 43.97, 0.44 * 43.97, 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 1.5, 1.5)
    fails = fails + mt_row("Q2 AUC 7.5 mg (ng h/mL) Qiu 2024       ", auc, 127.9, 0.34 * 127.9, 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 1.0, 1.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("Q3 Cmax 3 mg (ng/mL) Hohmann 2015      ", cmax * 3.0 / 7.5, 9.99, mdz_sd_ci(9.99, 8.05, 12.4, 16.0), 0.0, 0, 3.0, 4.5)
    fails = fails + mt_row("Q4 AUC 3 mg (ng h/mL) Hohmann 2015     ", auc * 3.0 / 7.5, 24.4, mdz_sd_ci(24.4, 20.4, 29.2, 16.0), 0.0, 0, 1.5, 3.5)
    fails = fails + mt_row("Q5 Tmax (h) Qiu 2024 median            ", (*m)[6], 0.51, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.5, 2.0)
    fails = fails + mt_vd_cas((*m)[5] / (*m)[4])
    fails = fails + mt_vd_hs((*m)[7])
    return fails
}

fn mt_sec_tab(m: &![f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("V2 TABLET (ka fitted to the pooled tablet Tmax; Ahonen 1995 is not in any fit)")
    let auc = (*m)[9] * 1000.0
    let cmax = (*m)[10] * 1000.0
    fails = fails + mt_row("T1 Cmax 7.5 mg (ng/mL) Ahonen 1995     ", cmax, 34.0, 5.0 * cd_sqrt(12.0), 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 1.5, 1.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("T2 AUC 7.5 mg (ng h/mL) Ahonen 1995    ", auc, 102.0, 10.0 * cd_sqrt(12.0), 0.0, 1, 0.0, 1.5)
    fails = fails + mt_vd_c15((*m)[15] * 1000.0)
    fails = fails + mt_vd_a15((*m)[14] * 1000.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("T5 Tmax (h) Ahonen 1995 median         ", (*m)[11], 1.25, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.5, 2.0)
    fails = fails + mt_vd_cat((*m)[10] / (*m)[9])
    fails = fails + mt_vd_ht((*m)[12])
    println("  dose proportionality 7.5 -> 15 mg (tablet Cmax): an identity of the linear model; Bornemann 1985")
    println("  (abstract only) found Cmax and AUC proportional between 7.5 and 15 mg, more than proportional at 30 mg")
    fails = fails + mt_rel("E10 Cmax(15)/Cmax(7.5) = 2", (*m)[15] / (*m)[10], 2.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("E10 AUC(15)/AUC(7.5) = 2", (*m)[14] / (*m)[9], 2.0, 1.0e-9)
    return fails
}

fn mt_sec_ext(d: &Circ28Drug, m: &![f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let fg = (*m)[18]
    let eh = (*m)[19]
    let eg = (*m)[20]
    let f_pred = fg * (1.0 - eh)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("guard: Fg (1 - Eh) here = F of the IV and solution runs (engine-dependent helper values)", f_pred, ((*m)[4] / 7.5) / (*m)[0], 2.0e-3)
    println("V3 both forms: IV half-life, extractions, oral F (E6-E9, and 3 of the 6 groups of E7, share their source with the Fg pool: not independent)")
    fails = fails + mt_vd_hiv((*m)[2])
    fails = fails + mt_row("E2 gut extraction after IV  Paine 1996 ", eg, 0.08, 0.11, 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 1.0, 1.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E3 Eh  Thummel 1996 (abstract)         ", eh, 0.44, 0.14, 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 2.0, 0.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E4 Eh  Hohmann 2015 (3 mg, CI to SD)   ", eh, 0.43, 4.0 * 0.12 / (2.0 * 2.1314), 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 2.0, 0.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E5 Fh = 1 - Eh  Gorski 1998            ", 1.0 - eh, 0.74, 0.1, 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 1.5, 0.5)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E6a Fg (pooled) vs Gorski 1998 [INPUT]  ", fg, 0.42, 0.2, 0.0, 2, 0.0, 2.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E6b Fg (pooled) vs Hohmann 3 mg 0.39 [INPUT]", fg, 0.39, 4.0 * 0.17 / (2.0 * 2.1314), 0.0, 2, 0.0, 2.0)
    fails = fails + mt_vd_f(f_pred)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E8 oral F  Gorski 1998 [Fg is an input]", f_pred, 0.31, 0.1, 0.0, 1, 0.0, 2.0)
    let fth = (1.0 - 0.44) * (1.0 - 0.43)
    let sth = cd_sqrt(0.57 * 0.14 * 0.57 * 0.14 + 0.56 * 0.24 * 0.56 * 0.24)
    fails = fails + mt_row("E9 oral F  Thummel (1-EH)(1-EG) [Fg input]", f_pred, fth, sth, 0.0, 1, 0.0 - 1.0, 2.0)
    return fails
}

// closed-form refit at a given ps_gut and Fg (no kernel run); prints Eg, Eh, F and AUC per mg
fn mt_sens(d: &Circ28Drug, psg: f64, fg: f64, gv: i32) -> f64 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    mt_fill(d, 0.0 - 1.0, &!th)
    th[CD_PSGUT] = psg
    let t = mdz_fit(th, mdz_obs_vss(), mdz_obs_cl(), fg, gv)
    var t2 = t
    let p = circ28_drug_params_theta(t2)
    let eg = circ28_gut_extraction(p)
    let eh = circ28_hepatic_extraction(p)
    let fgg = circ28_gut_availability(p)
    let f = fgg * (1.0 - eh)
    print("  ps_gut "); print(psg); print("  Fg "); print(fgg); print("  clint_gut "); print(t[CD_CLGUT]); print("  clint "); print(t[CD_CLINT])
    print("  Eg "); print(eg); print("  Eh "); print(eh); print("  F "); print(f)
    print("  AUC per mg "); println(1000.0 * f / mdz_obs_cl())
    return eg
}

fn mt_sec_sens(d: &Circ28Drug, gv: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S3 sensitivity, clint_gut and clint refitted each time (ka not refitted)")
    println("  Fg: 0.57 (Paine alone, round 3), pooled (record), 0.4808 (pool without Paine), 0.503, 0.42 (Gorski), 0.39 (Hohmann 3 mg), at ps_gut 10.454:")
    let psr = circ28_drug_value(d, CD_PSGUT)
    let e57 = mt_sens(d, psr, 0.57, gv)
    let epl = mt_sens(d, psr, mdz_obs_fg(), gv)
    let enp = mt_sens(d, psr, 0.4808, gv)
    let e50 = mt_sens(d, psr, 0.503, gv)
    let e42 = mt_sens(d, psr, 0.42, gv)
    let e39 = mt_sens(d, psr, 0.39, gv)
    println("  ps_gut (L/h) at the pooled Fg:")
    let p5 = mt_sens(d, 5.0, mdz_obs_fg(), gv)
    let p10 = mt_sens(d, 10.5, mdz_obs_fg(), gv)
    let p20 = mt_sens(d, 20.0, mdz_obs_fg(), gv)
    if !(e57 < e50 && e50 < epl && epl < enp && enp < e42 && e42 < e39) {
        println("  [FAIL] Eg must rise as Fg falls")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    if !(p5 < p10 && p10 < p20) {
        println("  [FAIL] Eg must rise with ps_gut")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    return fails
}

// is the peak held back by drug sitting in the gut tissue? Exit rates of the gut tissue
// compartment: back to the vascular pool ps/(kp Vt) and metabolism clint_gut fu/(kp Vt)
fn mt_sec_gut(d: &Circ28Drug, gv: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let p = mdz_params_rec(d, gv)
    let vt = p.v[8] * (1.0 - p.vf[8])
    let kps = p.ps[8] / (p.kp[8] * vt)
    let kmet = p.clint_gut * p.fu / (p.kp[8] * vt)
    let mrt = 1.0 / (kps + kmet)
    println("S4 gut-tissue hold-up (diagnostic for a too-low peak)")
    print("  gut tissue volume "); print(vt); print(" L  kp "); print(p.kp[8]); print("  exit rate to blood "); print(kps)
    print(" /h  metabolism "); print(kmet); print(" /h  mean residence time "); print(60.0 * mrt); println(" min")
    print("  absorption: MTT solution "); print(60.0 * 4.0 / mdz_ka_fit(0, gv)); print(" min (MTT = ntr/k), tablet "); print(60.0 * 4.0 / mdz_ka_fit(1, gv)); println(" min")
    if !(mrt < 0.25 * 4.0 / mdz_ka_fit(0, gv)) {
        println("  gut-tissue residence is not negligible against the solution MTT")
    } else {
        println("  gut-tissue residence is < 25% of the solution MTT: not the cause of a low peak")
    }
    return fails
}

fn mt_prn_budget(tag: string, b: &MdzBudget) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    print(tag); print(": "); print((*b).runs); println(" kernel runs")
    print("  AUC_oral "); print((*b).auc * 1000.0); print(" ng h/mL  u "); print(cd_sqrt((*b).var_auc) * 1000.0)
    print("  (rel "); print(cd_sqrt((*b).var_auc) / (*b).auc); println(")")
    print("  Cmax     "); print((*b).cmax * 1000.0); print(" ng/mL    u "); print(cd_sqrt((*b).var_cmax) * 1000.0)
    print("  (rel "); print(cd_sqrt((*b).var_cmax) / (*b).cmax); println(")")
    println("  input          u(input)      share of var(AUC) %   share of var(Cmax) %")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 9 {
        print("  "); print(mt_name(i)); print("   "); print((*b).u[i]); print("   "); print(100.0 * (*b).contrib_auc[i] / (*b).var_auc)
        print("   "); println(100.0 * (*b).contrib_cmax[i] / (*b).var_cmax)
        i = i + 1
    }
    let sl = (*b).sens_auc[5] * mdz_obs_cl() / (*b).auc
    print("  dlnAUC/dlnCL_obs (refit) = "); println(sl)
    if !(sl < 0.0 - 1.0 && sl > 0.0 - 2.0) {
        println("  [FAIL] sensitivity outside (-2,-1)")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

fn mt_sec_unc(u: &Circ28Unc) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    println("S5b record-level propagation, solution record (18 parameters independent, no refit)")
    print("  runs "); print((*u).runs); print("  AUC_oral "); print((*u).auc * 1000.0); print("  u "); print(cd_sqrt((*u).var_auc) * 1000.0)
    print("  Cmax "); print((*u).cmax * 1000.0); print("  u "); println(cd_sqrt((*u).var_cmax) * 1000.0)
    println("  parameter      share of var(AUC) %   share of var(Cmax) %")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 18 {
        if (*u).contrib_auc[i] > 0.0 || (*u).contrib_cmax[i] > 0.0 {
            print("  "); print(mt_rname(i)); print("   "); print(100.0 * (*u).contrib_auc[i] / (*u).var_auc)
            print("   "); println(100.0 * (*u).contrib_cmax[i] / (*u).var_cmax)
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 0
}


// ---- B. distribution diagnostic (round 4): which organs carry the terminal phase, and the ps scalar ----
fn mt_oname(i: i32) -> string {
    if i == 0 { return "blood (all vascular)" }
    if i == 1 { return "liver   " }
    if i == 2 { return "kidney  " }
    if i == 3 { return "brain   " }
    if i == 4 { return "heart   " }
    if i == 5 { return "lung    " }
    if i == 6 { return "muscle  " }
    if i == 7 { return "adipose " }
    if i == 8 { return "gut     " }
    if i == 9 { return "skin    " }
    if i == 10 { return "bone    " }
    if i == 11 { return "spleen  " }
    if i == 12 { return "pancreas" }
    return "rest    "
}

// shares of the body drug (fractions) at 4, 8, 12 h and the early plasma profile; returns 1 if the
// shares do not sum to 1 (identity)
fn mt_prn_dist(tag: string, f: &[f64; 48]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var bad = 0
    println(tag)
    println("      share of body drug      4 h        8 h        12 h")
    var o: i32 = 0
    while o < 14 {
        print("      "); print(mt_oname(o)); print("  "); print((*f)[o]); print("  "); print((*f)[14 + o]); print("  "); println((*f)[28 + o])
        o = o + 1
    }
    var j: i32 = 0
    while j < 3 {
        var sum = 0.0
        o = 0
        while o < 14 {
            sum = sum + (*f)[14 * j + o]
            o = o + 1
        }
        if mt_abs(sum - 1.0) > 1.0e-9 { bad = 1 }
        j = j + 1
    }
    print("      venous plasma mg/L per mg at 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 2 h: "); print((*f)[42]); print("  "); print((*f)[43]); print("  "); print((*f)[44]); print("  "); println((*f)[45])
    print("      C(2 h)/C(0.1 h) = "); print((*f)[45] / (*f)[42]); println("   (Heizmann 1983 abstract: about 0.10 within 2 h of a rapid injection; no n, SD or time of C0)")
    if bad == 1 { println("      [FAIL] shares do not sum to 1") }
    return bad
}

fn mt_psrow(tag: string, p: &[f64; 24], b: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    print("  "); print(tag); print(":  IV CL "); print(1.0 / (*p)[b]); print(" L/h  IV t1/2 "); print((*p)[b + 1])
    print(" h  tablet Cmax/AUC "); print((*p)[b + 3] / (*p)[b + 2]); print(" /h  tablet Tmax "); print((*p)[b + 4]); println(" h")
    return 0
}

fn mt_sec_ps(p: &[f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S6b response to the ps scalar (all organs' ps x scalar; NOTHING refitted, so CL moves too)")
    mt_psrow("ps x 0.3", p, 0)
    mt_psrow("ps x 1  ", p, 5)
    mt_psrow("ps x 3  ", p, 10)
    let t03 = (*p)[1]
    let t1 = (*p)[6]
    let t3 = (*p)[11]
    let r03 = (*p)[3] / (*p)[2]
    let r1 = (*p)[8] / (*p)[7]
    let r3 = (*p)[13] / (*p)[12]
    println("  predictions written before the run (header): t1/2(3x) 2.4-3.0, t1/2(0.3x) ~4.5; Cmax/AUC(3x) ~0.26, (0.3x) ~0.19")
    if t3 >= 2.4 && t3 <= 3.0 { println("      t1/2 at 3x: held") } else { println("      t1/2 at 3x: MISSED") }
    if t03 >= 4.0 && t03 <= 5.0 { println("      t1/2 at 0.3x: held") } else { println("      t1/2 at 0.3x: MISSED") }
    if r3 >= 0.24 && r3 <= 0.28 { println("      Cmax/AUC at 3x: held") } else { println("      Cmax/AUC at 3x: MISSED") }
    if r03 >= 0.17 && r03 <= 0.21 { println("      Cmax/AUC at 0.3x: held") } else { println("      Cmax/AUC at 0.3x: MISSED") }
    print("  observed IV t1/2 2.06 h (distribution, E1); tablet Cmax/AUC 0.359 (T6): the model at 3x gives "); print(t3); print(" h and "); println(r3)
    // direction (asserted): faster exchange shortens the terminal phase
    if !(t3 < t1 && t1 < t03) {
        println("  [FAIL] t1/2 must fall as ps rises")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    return fails
}

// perfusion-limited time constants of the two big tissues (organ i): tau = kp Vt / (Q bp), the time the
// blood flow needs to move the tissue's drug content at the tissue's plasma concentration
fn mt_tau(p: &Circ28Params, o: i32, nm: string) -> f64 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let vt = (*p).v[o] * (1.0 - (*p).vf[o])
    let tau = (*p).kp[o] * vt / ((*p).q[o] * (*p).bp)
    print("      "); print(nm); print(" kp "); print((*p).kp[o]); print("  tissue volume "); print(vt); print(" L  Q "); print((*p).q[o])
    print(" L/h  ps/Q "); print((*p).ps[o] / (*p).q[o]); print("  holds kp Vt "); print((*p).kp[o] * vt); print(" L-eq  tau_perfusion "); print(tau); println(" h")
    return tau
}

fn mt_sec_tau(d: &Circ28Drug, gv: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let p = mdz_params_rec(d, gv)
    println("S6c perfusion-limited time constants of the tissues that carry the terminal phase (ps scalar 1)")
    let ta = mt_tau(&p, 7, "adipose")
    let tm = mt_tau(&p, 6, "muscle ")
    println("      the terminal IV t1/2 is set by the slowest tissue, not by ps: ps/Q is large for both")
    return 0
}

fn mt_uka(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    return cd_sqrt(circ28_drug_variance(d, CD_KA))
}
fn mt_vslot(d: &Circ28Drug, i: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    return circ28_drug_value(d, i)
}
fn mt_vka(d: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    return circ28_drug_value(d, CD_KA)
}

fn mt_sec_bud(d: &Circ28Drug, form: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let b = mdz_budget(d, 7.5, form, mdz_gv_adopted())
    if form == 0 { return mt_prn_budget("S5a solution", &b) }
    return mt_prn_budget("S5c tablet", &b)
}

fn mt_sec_unc2(d: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let c75 = mdz_cfg_oral(7.5)
    let u = mdz_drug_unc(d, c75, mdz_gv_adopted())
    return mt_sec_unc(&u)
}


// ---- ROUND 5 sections: both gut-wall Kp variants side by side, stage-count sweep, MTT -------------------------
// z of a row with an inter-individual SD
fn mt_zs(pred: f64, obs: f64, sd: f64) -> f64 with Div {
    return (pred - obs) / sd
}

// z of a distribution row: which 0 oral F, 1 Cmax 15 mg, 2 AUC 15 mg, 3 solution Cmax/AUC, 4 tablet Cmax/AUC,
// 5 solution oral t1/2, 6 tablet oral t1/2, 7 IV t1/2 (the groups are the mt_l_* lists above)
fn mt_zd(pred: f64, which: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var m: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var n: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var s: [f64; 8] = [0.0; 8]
    var k: i32 = 0
    if which == 0 { k = mt_l_f(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 1 { k = mt_l_c15(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 2 { k = mt_l_a15(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 3 { k = mt_l_cas(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 4 { k = mt_l_cat(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 5 { k = mt_l_hs(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 6 { k = mt_l_ht(&!m, &!n) }
    if which == 7 { k = mt_l_hiv(&!m, &!n) }
    let q = mdz_pool(&m, &s, &n, k)
    return (pred - q.mean) / q.sb
}

fn mt_cname(i: i32) -> string {
    if i == 0 { return "Q1 solution Cmax 7.5 mg  [peak]" }
    if i == 1 { return "Q2 solution AUC 7.5 mg        " }
    if i == 2 { return "Q3 solution Cmax 3 mg   [peak]" }
    if i == 3 { return "Q4 solution AUC 3 mg          " }
    if i == 4 { return "Q5 solution Tmax / 0.51 h (fit)" }
    if i == 5 { return "Q6 solution Cmax/AUC    [peak]" }
    if i == 6 { return "Q7 solution oral t1/2         " }
    if i == 7 { return "T1 tablet Cmax 7.5 mg   [peak]" }
    if i == 8 { return "T2 tablet AUC 7.5 mg          " }
    if i == 9 { return "T3 tablet Cmax 15 mg    [peak]" }
    if i == 10 { return "T4 tablet AUC 15 mg           " }
    if i == 11 { return "T6 tablet Cmax/AUC     [peak]" }
    if i == 12 { return "T7 tablet oral t1/2           " }
    if i == 13 { return "E1 IV t1/2                    " }
    if i == 14 { return "E2 gut extraction after IV    " }
    if i == 15 { return "E3 Eh Thummel                 " }
    if i == 16 { return "E4 Eh Hohmann                 " }
    if i == 17 { return "E5 Fh Gorski                  " }
    if i == 18 { return "E7 oral F, 6 groups           " }
    if i == 19 { return "E8 oral F Gorski              " }
    return "E9 oral F Thummel (1-EH)(1-EG)  "
}

// the 21 validation statistics of one column (m as filled in main); z[4] is a ratio, not a z
fn mt_cols(m: &[f64; 24], z: &![f64; 24]) -> i32 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let auc = (*m)[4] * 1000.0
    let cmax = (*m)[5] * 1000.0
    (*z)[0] = mt_zs(cmax, 43.97, 0.44 * 43.97)
    (*z)[1] = mt_zs(auc, 127.9, 0.34 * 127.9)
    (*z)[2] = mt_zs(cmax * 3.0 / 7.5, 9.99, mdz_sd_ci(9.99, 8.05, 12.4, 16.0))
    (*z)[3] = mt_zs(auc * 3.0 / 7.5, 24.4, mdz_sd_ci(24.4, 20.4, 29.2, 16.0))
    (*z)[4] = (*m)[6] / 0.51
    (*z)[5] = mt_zd((*m)[5] / (*m)[4], 3)
    (*z)[6] = mt_zd((*m)[7], 5)
    let auct = (*m)[9] * 1000.0
    let cmaxt = (*m)[10] * 1000.0
    (*z)[7] = mt_zs(cmaxt, 34.0, 5.0 * cd_sqrt(12.0))
    (*z)[8] = mt_zs(auct, 102.0, 10.0 * cd_sqrt(12.0))
    (*z)[9] = mt_zd((*m)[15] * 1000.0, 1)
    (*z)[10] = mt_zd((*m)[14] * 1000.0, 2)
    (*z)[11] = mt_zd((*m)[10] / (*m)[9], 4)
    (*z)[12] = mt_zd((*m)[12], 6)
    (*z)[13] = mt_zd((*m)[2], 7)
    (*z)[14] = mt_zs((*m)[20], 0.08, 0.11)
    (*z)[15] = mt_zs((*m)[19], 0.44, 0.14)
    (*z)[16] = mt_zs((*m)[19], 0.43, 4.0 * 0.12 / (2.0 * 2.1314))
    (*z)[17] = mt_zs(1.0 - (*m)[19], 0.74, 0.1)
    let fp = (*m)[18] * (1.0 - (*m)[19])
    (*z)[18] = mt_zd(fp, 0)
    (*z)[19] = mt_zs(fp, 0.31, 0.1)
    let fth = (1.0 - 0.44) * (1.0 - 0.43)
    let sth = cd_sqrt(0.57 * 0.14 * 0.57 * 0.14 + 0.56 * 0.24 * 0.56 * 0.24)
    (*z)[20] = mt_zs(fp, fth, sth)
    return 0
}

fn mt_vrd(z: f64) -> string {
    if mt_abs(z) <= 2.0 { return "P" }
    return "F"
}

// the adoption rule written in the header: returns 1 if the gut-unscaled column (b) is to be adopted
fn mt_decide(za: &[f64; 24], zb: &[f64; 24], auca: f64, aucb: f64, uauc: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var best = 0.0
    var br: i32 = 0 - 1
    var flip = false
    var j: i32 = 0
    while j < 6 {
        var r: i32 = 0
        if j == 0 { r = 0 }
        if j == 1 { r = 2 }
        if j == 2 { r = 5 }
        if j == 3 { r = 7 }
        if j == 4 { r = 9 }
        if j == 5 { r = 11 }
        if mt_abs((*za)[r]) > 2.0 {
            if mt_abs((*za)[r]) > best {
                best = mt_abs((*za)[r])
                br = r
            }
            if mt_abs((*zb)[r]) <= 2.0 { flip = true }
        }
        j = j + 1
    }
    var c1 = flip
    if br >= 0 {
        if best - mt_abs((*zb)[br]) > 0.5 { c1 = true }
    }
    var c2 = true
    var r2: i32 = 0
    while r2 < 21 {
        if r2 != 4 {
            if mt_abs((*za)[r2]) <= 2.0 && mt_abs((*zb)[r2]) > 2.0 { c2 = false }
        }
        r2 = r2 + 1
    }
    let c3 = mt_abs(aucb - auca) < uauc
    print("  rule (i) a failing peak row improves by > 0.5 |z| or flips to PASS: ")
    if c1 { println("yes") } else { println("no") }
    print("  rule (ii) no row changes from PASS to FAIL: ")
    if c2 { println("yes") } else { println("no") }
    print("  rule (iii) AUC 7.5 mg (solution) moves by less than u(AUC) "); print(uauc); print(" ng h/mL: |diff| "); print(mt_abs(aucb - auca))
    if c3 { println("  yes") } else { println("  no") }
    if c1 && c2 && c3 { return 1 }
    return 0
}

fn mt_uauc(b: &MdzBudget) -> f64 with Mut, Div {
    return cd_sqrt((*b).var_auc) * 1000.0
}

fn mt_sec_cols(a: &[f64; 24], b: &[f64; 24], uauc: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    var za: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    var zb: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    mt_cols(a, &!za)
    mt_cols(b, &!zb)
    println("G both gut-wall Kp variants, whole validation (column 0: all-organ scalar, column 1: gut wall at its Rodgers-Rowland Kp, scalar refitted to V_ss)")
    print("  V_ss scalar            "); print((*a)[21]); print("   "); println((*b)[21])
    print("  k solution (/h)        "); print((*a)[17]); print("   "); println((*b)[17])
    print("  k tablet (/h)          "); print((*a)[22]); print("   "); println((*b)[22])
    print("  MTT solution 4/k (h)   "); print(4.0 / (*a)[17]); print("   "); println(4.0 / (*b)[17])
    print("  MTT tablet 4/k (h)     "); print(4.0 / (*a)[22]); print("   "); println(4.0 / (*b)[22])
    print("  IV t1/2 (h)            "); print((*a)[2]); print("   "); println((*b)[2])
    print("  IV AUC_inf (ng h/mL per mg) "); print((*a)[0] * 1000.0); print("   "); println((*b)[0] * 1000.0)
    print("  solution 7.5 mg: AUC "); print((*a)[4] * 1000.0); print("   "); print((*b)[4] * 1000.0); print("   Cmax "); print((*a)[5] * 1000.0); print("   "); println((*b)[5] * 1000.0)
    print("  tablet   7.5 mg: AUC "); print((*a)[9] * 1000.0); print("   "); print((*b)[9] * 1000.0); print("   Cmax "); print((*a)[10] * 1000.0); print("   "); println((*b)[10] * 1000.0)
    print("  Cmax/AUC solution      "); print((*a)[5] / (*a)[4]); print("   "); println((*b)[5] / (*b)[4])
    print("  Cmax/AUC tablet        "); print((*a)[10] / (*a)[9]); print("   "); println((*b)[10] / (*b)[9])
    print("  oral t1/2 solution     "); print((*a)[7]); print("   "); println((*b)[7])
    println("  row                               z (col 0)   z (col 1)   verdict 0 / 1")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 21 {
        print("  "); print(mt_cname(i)); print("   "); print(za[i]); print("   "); print(zb[i])
        if i == 4 {
            println("   (ratio, fitted)")
        } else {
            print("   "); print(mt_vrd(za[i])); print(" / "); println(mt_vrd(zb[i]))
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    let dec = mt_decide(&za, &zb, (*a)[4] * 1000.0, (*b)[4] * 1000.0, uauc)
    print("  adoption rule gives: ")
    if dec == 1 { println("ADOPT the gut-unscaled variant") } else { println("KEEP the all-organ scalar") }
    if dec != mdz_gv_adopted() {
        println("  [FAIL] the module's adopted variant is not the one the rule gives")
        fails = fails + 1
    }
    return fails
}

// MTT = ntr / k of each dose form against Brill 2014 (validation only, different populations)
fn mt_sec_mtt(a: &[f64; 24], b: &[f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("M mean transit time MTT = ntr / k against Brill 2014 (PMC4171595, full text): tablet, 20 morbidly obese patients, Ktr 0.057 /min,")
    println("  MTT 70.2 min = 1.17 h; ORAL SOLUTION, 12 healthy volunteers, Ktr 0.130 /min, MTT 30.8 min = 0.51 h. Populations differ: validation only")
    fails = fails + mt_row("M1 tablet MTT (h), gv 0                 ", 4.0 / (*a)[22], 1.17, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.5, 1.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("M2 solution MTT (h), gv 0               ", 4.0 / (*a)[17], 0.51, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.5, 1.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("M1 tablet MTT (h), gv 1                 ", 4.0 / (*b)[22], 1.17, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.5, 1.0)
    fails = fails + mt_row("M2 solution MTT (h), gv 1               ", 4.0 / (*b)[17], 0.51, 0.0, 2.0, 1, 0.5, 1.0)
    return fails
}

// one run for the stage-count sweep (gv 0 record d): form 0 solution, 1 tablet; k 0 Cmax, 1 Tmax, 2 AUC_inf
fn mt_msw(d: &Circ28Drug, form: i32, ntr: i32, k: i32) -> f64 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var th: [f64; 18] = [0.0; 18]
    mt_fill(d, 0.0 - 1.0, &!th)
    th[CD_KA] = mdz_k_sweep(form, ntr)
    var d2 = mdz_cfg_oral_n(1.0, ntr)
    let r = mdz_run_theta(th, d2, 0)
    if k == 0 { return r.cmax }
    if k == 1 { return r.tmax }
    return r.auc_inf
}

// sw[15 form + 3 (ntr - 1) + k]
fn mt_sec_sweep(sw: &[f64; 30], a: &[f64; 24]) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    println("S7 stage-count sweep (gv 0; k refitted to the pooled Tmax of each form at every ntr, offline bisection, stored in mdz_k_sweep)")
    println("  form      ntr   k (/h)   MTT=ntr/k (h)   Tmax (h)   Cmax/AUC (/h)   z vs observed distribution")
    var form: i32 = 0
    while form < 2 {
        var ntr: i32 = 1
        var prev = 0.0
        while ntr < 6 {
            let b = 15 * form + 3 * (ntr - 1)
            let ratio = (*sw)[b] / (*sw)[b + 2]
            let k = mdz_k_sweep(form, ntr)
            var z = 0.0
            if form == 0 { z = mt_zd(ratio, 3) } else { z = mt_zd(ratio, 4) }
            if form == 0 { print("  solution  ") } else { print("  tablet    ") }
            print(ntr); print("     "); print(k); print("   "); print((ntr as f64) / k); print("   "); print((*sw)[b + 1]); print("   "); print(ratio); print("   "); println(z)
            var tobs = mdz_obs_tmax(0)
            if form == 1 { tobs = mdz_obs_tmax(1) }
            fails = fails + mt_rel("   Tmax = pooled Tmax of the form", (*sw)[b + 1], tobs, 3.0e-3)
            if !(ratio > prev) {
                println("  [FAIL] Cmax/AUC must rise with the stage count")
                fails = fails + 1
            }
            prev = ratio
            ntr = ntr + 1
        }
        form = form + 1
    }
    let b4 = 15 + 3 * 3
    fails = fails + mt_rel("guard: tablet sweep at ntr 4 = the tablet run of the all-organ column (Cmax per mg)", (*sw)[b4], (*a)[10] / 7.5, 2.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("guard: solution sweep at ntr 4 = the solution run of the all-organ column (Cmax per mg)", (*sw)[9], (*a)[5] / 7.5, 2.0e-3)
    return fails
}


fn main() -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let gv = mdz_gv_adopted()
    let gx = 1 - gv
    var d = circ28_drug_new()
    mdz_drug_into(&!d, gv)
    var dx = circ28_drug_new()
    mdz_drug_into(&!dx, gx)
    // Every kernel run is made here, at the shallowest call depth (lean_single returns wrong run
    // results from deeper frames); the scalars go to the sections in one array.
    // 0-3 IV 1 mg: AUC, Cmax, t1/2, balance; 4-8 oral 7.5 mg solution: AUC, Cmax, Tmax, t1/2, balance;
    // 9-13 the same, tablet; 14-15 tablet 15 mg: AUC, Cmax; 16 u(k solution); 17 k solution;
    // 18-20 Fg, Eh, Eg (closed forms); 21 V_ss scalar; 22 k tablet; 23 hepatic clint.
    // m is the ADOPTED variant gv, mx the other one (gx).
    var m: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    var mx: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    let u = 0.0 - 1.0
    m[0] = mt_m0(&d, u, 0, gv)
    m[1] = mt_m0(&d, u, 1, gv)
    m[2] = mt_m0(&d, u, 3, gv)
    m[3] = mt_m0(&d, u, 4, gv)
    m[4] = mt_m1(&d, u, 0, gv)
    m[5] = mt_m1(&d, u, 1, gv)
    m[6] = mt_m1(&d, u, 2, gv)
    m[7] = mt_m1(&d, u, 3, gv)
    m[8] = mt_m1(&d, u, 4, gv)
    let bud_s = mdz_budget(&d, 7.5, 0, gv)
    let c75 = mdz_cfg_oral(7.5)
    let unc = mdz_drug_unc(&d, c75, gv)
    m[18] = mt_fg(&d)
    m[19] = mt_eh(&d)
    m[20] = mt_eg(&d)
    m[16] = mt_uka(&d)
    m[17] = mt_vka(&d)
    m[21] = mt_vslot(&d, CD_KPSC)
    m[23] = mt_vslot(&d, CD_CLINT)
    mdz_ka_record(&!d, 1, gv)
    m[22] = mt_vka(&d)
    m[9] = mt_m1(&d, u, 0, gv)
    m[10] = mt_m1(&d, u, 1, gv)
    m[11] = mt_m1(&d, u, 2, gv)
    m[12] = mt_m1(&d, u, 3, gv)
    m[13] = mt_m1(&d, u, 4, gv)
    m[14] = mt_m2(&d, u, 0, gv)
    m[15] = mt_m2(&d, u, 1, gv)
    let bud_t = mdz_budget(&d, 7.5, 1, gv)
    // the other Kp variant: the same runs, no budgets
    mx[0] = mt_m0(&dx, u, 0, gx)
    mx[1] = mt_m0(&dx, u, 1, gx)
    mx[2] = mt_m0(&dx, u, 3, gx)
    mx[3] = mt_m0(&dx, u, 4, gx)
    mx[4] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 0, gx)
    mx[5] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 1, gx)
    mx[6] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 2, gx)
    mx[7] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 3, gx)
    mx[8] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 4, gx)
    mx[18] = mt_fg(&dx)
    mx[19] = mt_eh(&dx)
    mx[20] = mt_eg(&dx)
    mx[16] = mt_uka(&dx)
    mx[17] = mt_vka(&dx)
    mx[21] = mt_vslot(&dx, CD_KPSC)
    mx[23] = mt_vslot(&dx, CD_CLINT)
    mdz_ka_record(&!dx, 1, gx)
    mx[22] = mt_vka(&dx)
    mx[9] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 0, gx)
    mx[10] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 1, gx)
    mx[11] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 2, gx)
    mx[12] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 3, gx)
    mx[13] = mt_m1(&dx, u, 4, gx)
    mx[14] = mt_m2(&dx, u, 0, gx)
    mx[15] = mt_m2(&dx, u, 1, gx)
    // stage-count sweep on the all-organ record (gv 0): 30 runs
    var sw: [f64; 30] = [0.0; 30]
    var swf: i32 = 0
    while swf < 2 {
        var swn: i32 = 1
        while swn < 6 {
            var swk: i32 = 0
            while swk < 3 {
                if gv == 0 {
                    sw[15 * swf + 3 * (swn - 1) + swk] = mt_msw(&d, swf, swn, swk)
                } else {
                    sw[15 * swf + 3 * (swn - 1) + swk] = mt_msw(&dx, swf, swn, swk)
                }
                swk = swk + 1
            }
            swn = swn + 1
        }
        swf = swf + 1
    }
    fails = fails + mt_sec_pool()
    fails = fails + mt_sec_fit(&d, &!m, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_iv(&d, &!m, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_sol(&!m)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_tab(&!m)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_ext(&d, &!m)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_sens(&d, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_gut(&d, gv)
    println("S5 uncertainty budgets, 7.5 mg oral, pooled uncertainties, refit at every perturbation (k refitted to Tmax by one chord step)")
    fails = fails + mt_prn_budget("S5a solution", &bud_s)
    fails = fails + mt_prn_budget("S5c tablet", &bud_t)
    println("S5d the budgets' central values are the direct runs (guards the engine-dependent frame quirks)")
    fails = fails + mt_rel("budget AUC solution = run", bud_s.auc, m[4], 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("budget Cmax solution = run", bud_s.cmax, m[5], 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("budget AUC tablet = run", bud_t.auc, m[9], 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_rel("budget Cmax tablet = run", bud_t.cmax, m[10], 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_unc(&unc)
    // S6, round 4 diagnostic: the record is the tablet one here. One organ-share run per ps scalar
    // (mdz_iv_dist), then the IV and tablet scalars: p[5 b + 0 .. 4] = IV AUC_inf, IV t1/2,
    // tablet AUC, tablet Cmax, tablet Tmax for b = 0 (ps x 0.3), 1 (x 1), 2 (x 3).
    println("S6 which organs carry the terminal phase (IV 1 mg, record ps scalar 1)")
    var fd: [f64; 48] = [0.0; 48]
    var pr: [f64; 24] = [0.0; 24]
    mdz_iv_dist(&d, 0.0 - 1.0, &!fd, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_prn_dist("S6a ps x 1 (record)", &fd)
    mdz_iv_dist(&d, 0.3, &!fd, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_prn_dist("S6a ps x 0.3", &fd)
    mdz_iv_dist(&d, 3.0, &!fd, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_prn_dist("S6a ps x 3", &fd)
    pr[0] = mt_m0(&d, 0.3, 0, gv)
    pr[1] = mt_m0(&d, 0.3, 3, gv)
    pr[2] = mt_m1(&d, 0.3, 0, gv)
    pr[3] = mt_m1(&d, 0.3, 1, gv)
    pr[4] = mt_m1(&d, 0.3, 2, gv)
    pr[5] = mt_m0(&d, 1.0, 0, gv)
    pr[6] = mt_m0(&d, 1.0, 3, gv)
    pr[7] = mt_m1(&d, 1.0, 0, gv)
    pr[8] = mt_m1(&d, 1.0, 1, gv)
    pr[9] = mt_m1(&d, 1.0, 2, gv)
    pr[10] = mt_m0(&d, 3.0, 0, gv)
    pr[11] = mt_m0(&d, 3.0, 3, gv)
    pr[12] = mt_m1(&d, 3.0, 0, gv)
    pr[13] = mt_m1(&d, 3.0, 1, gv)
    pr[14] = mt_m1(&d, 3.0, 2, gv)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_ps(&pr)
    fails = fails + mt_sec_tau(&d, gv)
    // round 5
    let uauc = mt_uauc(&bud_s)
    if gv == 0 {
        fails = fails + mt_sec_cols(&m, &mx, uauc)
        fails = fails + mt_sec_mtt(&m, &mx)
        fails = fails + mt_sec_sweep(&sw, &m)
    } else {
        fails = fails + mt_sec_cols(&mx, &m, uauc)
        fails = fails + mt_sec_mtt(&mx, &m)
        fails = fails + mt_sec_sweep(&sw, &mx)
    }
    if fails == 0 {
        println("CIRC28_DRUG_MIDAZOLAM_PASS")
        return 0
    }
    println("CIRC28_DRUG_MIDAZOLAM_FAIL")
    return 1
}
